Title: Prune the native Claude memory stores of projects that adopted memory v8
Created: 2026-11-09
Author: reviewer

--- log ---
2026-11-09T13:53Z reviewer created

--- body ---
## Context
The 2026-11-09 memory v8 deployments consolidated each project's Claude Code native memory store
(`~/.claude/projects/<cwd-key>/memory/`) into the project's own `memory/` but left the native
stores untouched and still loading, by design: pruning is the author's call. Stores left live:
fuzzy-corpus (15 notes, PR fuzzy-corpus#68), chemin-de-voix (59, Tracing-Kieu#179),
aedist-technical-report (197, aedist-technical-report#1187). Earlier deployments (JETP-observer,
climate-finance-het, sen-causal-reading) may be in the same state; padme's was triaged and pruned
on 2026-11-07, which is the model. Each project's `memory/SOURCES.md` lists every note with its
disposition and blob id, so pruning loses nothing the repo did not keep or deliberately drop.
Related: 1480 stops publishing the harness's copies of these stores under `projects/`.

## Work
For each project that has adopted v8: read its SOURCES.md, triage the native notes (consolidated
-> delete; deliberately excluded personal or private -> author decides; harness-generic -> drop),
then prune the native store as padme was. Codex and Pi stores: confirm none exists per project.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] every v8 project's native store is pruned, or the author kept it on purpose (noted)
- [ ] no consolidated fact exists only in a native store
